# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify redirects for KaliNova.
#
# The app is a single-page application: every clean route is served by
# frontend/index.html and rendered by frontend/router.js. app/server.js does the
# same thing for the Docker/Express deployment, so both hosting models behave
# identically.
#
# Static files (css, js, images, icons) are matched first and are never
# rewritten, so existing links to /style.css or /assets/... keep working.
#
# Note: there is deliberately no redirect for /stories/<id> -> /blog/<slug>.
# A slug cannot be derived from a numeric id without a database lookup, so the
# frontend resolves the id and upgrades the URL in the browser instead. A static
# 301 here would send crawlers to a URL that does not exist.
#
# Note: the admin area is NOT part of this static deployment. /admin/login and
# /admin/dashboard are rendered by app/server.js against PostgreSQL, so on
# Cloudflare Pages they must fall through to the 404 below instead of the SPA
# shell (they are Disallowed in robots.txt). Serve the admin area from the
# Express deployment, or put /admin behind access control at the edge.

# Everything that is not a real file falls through to the SPA shell.
/*                        /index.html          200